1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,700
Hello again!

2
00:00:01,320 --> 00:00:05,560
Last time, in Beat the Beads, you remembered all eighteen formulas.

3
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:08,680
I promised you a brand new kind of trick.

4
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:12,040
One that adds and takes away, both at once.

5
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:14,440
Today, it is here.

6
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:17,080
It helps when the big friend gets stuck.

7
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:24,640
A reminder: the big friend takes the friend off the ones rod, then carries one bead to the tens rod.

8
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:25,900
You tell me.

9
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:27,860
What is six's big friend?

10
00:00:31,180 --> 00:00:31,780
Four!

11
00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:33,500
But here is a problem.

12
00:00:34,140 --> 00:00:37,000
Sometimes the ones rod cannot give the friend away.

13
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:41,260
There are not enough lower beads showing, and the upper bead is down.

14
00:00:41,880 --> 00:00:43,940
Then the big friend alone gets stuck.

15
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:45,500
We need something more.

16
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:48,140
Good news.

17
00:00:48,680 --> 00:00:49,900
The small friend can help.

18
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:54,140
Four's small friend is one, and four and one make five.

19
00:00:54,580 --> 00:00:57,660
The big friend and the small friend, working together.

20
00:00:58,080 --> 00:00:59,760
That is called the family.

21
00:01:00,780 --> 00:01:02,740
So, look at the ones rod first.

22
00:01:03,360 --> 00:01:06,360
If the big friend gets stuck like that, call the family.

23
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:09,180
Let us see it.

24
00:01:09,780 --> 00:01:10,800
Seven plus six.

25
00:01:11,640 --> 00:01:13,220
Make seven on the ones rod.

26
00:01:13,660 --> 00:01:15,940
Push two lower beads up with your thumb.

27
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:19,800
Then push the upper bead down with your index finger.

28
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:24,240
Remember: up is the thumb, and down is the index finger.

29
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:28,940
Six's friend is four, so take away four.

30
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:31,420
How many lower beads can we take away?

31
00:01:34,220 --> 00:01:35,260
Only two!

32
00:01:35,860 --> 00:01:36,760
We need four.

33
00:01:37,220 --> 00:01:39,680
The big friend is stuck, just like we said.

34
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:44,680
Plus six equals minus four, plus ten.

35
00:01:45,180 --> 00:01:47,320
But the small friend can take away four.

36
00:01:47,740 --> 00:01:49,700
Add one, then take away five.

37
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:53,440
Minus four equals plus one, minus five.

38
00:01:54,920 --> 00:01:56,180
Put them together.

39
00:01:56,700 --> 00:01:58,780
Here is the family trick for adding.

40
00:01:59,580 --> 00:02:03,640
Plus six equals plus one, minus five, plus ten.

41
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:07,000
Why?

42
00:02:07,620 --> 00:02:11,080
Plus ten adds four too many, so we take four away.

43
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:12,960
Remember our rule.

44
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:16,680
Ones rod first, and lower beads before the upper bead.

45
00:02:17,260 --> 00:02:17,940
Plus one.

46
00:02:18,380 --> 00:02:19,860
Push one lower bead up.

47
00:02:20,340 --> 00:02:20,680
Thumb!

48
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:23,560
Minus five.

49
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:25,200
Push the upper bead up.

50
00:02:25,620 --> 00:02:26,100
Thumb again!

51
00:02:27,020 --> 00:02:27,500
Oh!

52
00:02:27,780 --> 00:02:29,280
Only three on the ones rod?

53
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:30,900
Watch what happens next.

54
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:33,940
Now carry one bead to the tens rod.

55
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:35,420
And there it is.

56
00:02:35,940 --> 00:02:37,740
Seven plus six is thirteen!

57
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:40,380
That is our first family formula.

58
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:43,700
Having fun with the family?

59
00:02:44,420 --> 00:02:47,600
Give this video a like, and subscribe to meet the rest.

60
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:49,620
Bigger numbers now.

61
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:51,100
Make twenty-six.

62
00:02:51,860 --> 00:02:55,260
On the ones rod, one lower bead and the upper bead.

63
00:02:55,740 --> 00:02:57,860
Then two lower beads on the tens rod.

64
00:02:58,460 --> 00:03:00,400
Thumb up, index finger down!

65
00:03:01,300 --> 00:03:02,720
Seven's friend is three.

66
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:05,120
Can we take away three lower beads?

67
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:09,120
No!

68
00:03:09,760 --> 00:03:10,620
Only one.

69
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:12,080
Stuck again.

70
00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:13,400
Call the family.

71
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:17,920
Plus seven equals plus two, minus five, plus ten.

72
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:22,420
Push two lower beads up.

73
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:25,480
Now push the upper bead up.

74
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:28,640
Carry one bead to the tens rod.

75
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:30,280
Thumb all the way!

76
00:03:30,820 --> 00:03:32,800
Twenty-six plus seven is thirty-three!

77
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:34,600
Look.

78
00:03:35,060 --> 00:03:39,340
Every time: plus some lower beads, minus five, plus ten.

79
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:41,300
Every move went up.

80
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:43,380
So every move was a thumb.

81
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:46,080
Plus six, add one.

82
00:03:46,580 --> 00:03:48,180
Plus seven, add two.

83
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:50,380
Plus eight, add three.

84
00:03:50,860 --> 00:03:52,560
Plus nine, add four.

85
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:56,440
But minus five, and plus ten, never change.

86
00:03:59,260 --> 00:04:04,560
Four family formulas for adding: plus six, seven, eight and nine.

87
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:06,480
Your turn.

88
00:04:06,900 --> 00:04:08,500
Make five on the ones rod.

89
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:09,860
Just the upper bead.

90
00:04:10,220 --> 00:04:12,580
That is down, so use your index finger.

91
00:04:12,940 --> 00:04:14,060
Then add nine.

92
00:04:14,740 --> 00:04:15,880
What is nine's friend?

93
00:04:18,780 --> 00:04:19,420
One!

94
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:21,120
Look at the ones rod.

95
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:23,280
There are no lower beads at all.

96
00:04:23,580 --> 00:04:24,540
So call the family.

97
00:04:25,280 --> 00:04:27,260
Nine is how many more than five?

98
00:04:30,280 --> 00:04:30,920
Four!

99
00:04:31,460 --> 00:04:35,280
Plus nine equals plus four, minus five, plus ten.

100
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:38,860
Now do all three moves.

101
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:42,360
Ones rod first, and remember, up is the thumb.

102
00:04:43,940 --> 00:04:45,660
What number is showing now?

103
00:04:48,540 --> 00:04:50,700
Five plus nine is fourteen!

104
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:52,060
Well done!

105
00:04:52,540 --> 00:04:54,760
You did the family trick all by yourself.

106
00:04:55,620 --> 00:04:58,340
So now you know the family trick for adding.

107
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:00,640
Try them at home on your own abacus.

108
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:06,160
To meet the whole family, search for Abacus Kids on the Apple App Store or Google Play.

109
00:05:06,440 --> 00:05:07,300
Download it free.

110
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:10,640
Next time, the family works the other way round.

111
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:13,300
We will learn the family trick for taking away.

112
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:14,620
See you next time!
